## 6. Cross-Server Validation

### 6.1 Security Validation
- [ ] 6.1.1 Verify all default credentials have been changed
- [ ] 6.1.2 Confirm proper authentication is enabled for all services
- [ ] 6.1.3 Check SSL/TLS configuration where appropriate
- [ ] 6.1.4 Verify network security (firewall rules, port exposure)
- [ ] 6.1.5 Validate credential rotation procedures

### 6.2 Monitoring Integration
- [ ] 6.2.1 Verify Prometheus is collecting metrics from all servers
- [ ] 6.2.2 Confirm all exporters are reporting to Prometheus
- [ ] 6.2.3 Validate all Grafana datasources are functional
- [ ] 6.2.4 Check composite dashboards showing multiple server metrics
- [ ] 6.2.5 Test alerting for cross-server scenarios

### 6.3 Backup System Validation
- [ ] 6.3.1 Verify backup directories are configured
- [ ] 6.3.2 Check that backup schedules are established
- [ ] 6.3.3 Validate a recent backup exists for each critical component
- [ ] 6.3.4 Test a sample backup restore procedure for each database type
- [ ] 6.3.5 Verify backup retention policies are implemented

## 7. Performance Validation

### 7.1 Load Testing
- [ ] 7.1.1 Run basic performance tests on each database
- [ ] 7.1.2 Test concurrent operations on key databases
- [ ] 7.1.3 Benchmark query performance
- [ ] 7.1.4 Test recovery from simulated failures

### 7.2 Resource Monitoring
- [ ] 7.2.1 Verify system resource utilization is within expected parameters
- [ ] 7.2.2 Check for any bottlenecks or performance issues
- [ ] 7.2.3 Validate metrics against specified baselines
- [ ] 7.2.4 Monitor for any resource contention issues

## 8. Documentation Validation

### 8.1 Documentation Completeness
- [ ] 8.1.1 Confirm all required documentation is present
- [ ] 8.1.2 Check for accuracy in connection details
- [ ] 8.1.3 Verify recovery procedures are documented
- [ ] 8.1.4 Validate maintenance procedures are clearly defined
- [ ] 8.1.5 Ensure troubleshooting guides are available

### 8.2 Documentation Accessibility
- [ ] 8.2.1 Confirm documentation is properly organized
- [ ] 8.2.2 Verify documentation is version controlled
- [ ] 8.2.3 Check for proper formatting and readability
- [ ] 8.2.4 Validate cross-references and links

## 9. Final Validation & Report Generation

### 9.1 Validation Matrix
- [ ] 9.1.1 Create a validation matrix tracking each component's status
- [ ] 9.1.2 Document any discrepancies or issues found
- [ ] 9.1.3 Highlight successful validations
- [ ] 9.1.4 Flag any components requiring attention

### 9.2 Final Report
- [ ] 9.2.1 Generate a comprehensive validation report
- [ ] 9.2.2 Provide recommendations for any unresolved issues
- [ ] 9.2.3 Create executive summary of findings
- [ ] 9.2.4 Document lessons learned and best practices

## Success Criteria

1. All 29 database and monitoring components successfully validated as operational
2. Cross-server connectivity and authentication confirmed working properly
3. Monitoring system collecting metrics from all servers and components
4. Data storage properly configured on mounted disks
5. All systemd services configured for automatic startup
6. Backup procedures established and tested successfully
7. All systems passing security validation
8. Documentation complete, comprehensive, and accurate

## Validation Tools

1. A validation script will be created to automate verification of:
   - Service status for all components
   - Connection tests
   - Port availability checks
   - Basic functionality tests

2. Manual testing will be performed for:
   - Complex integrations
   - Security aspects
   - Performance characteristics
   - Backup and recovery scenarios

## Estimated Timeline

- Server Infrastructure Validation: 1 day
- Component Validation (all servers): 3 days
- Cross-Server Validation: 1 day
- Performance Validation: 1 day
- Documentation Validation: 1 day
- Final Report Generation: 1 day

Total: 7 days

## Appendix: Validation Scripts

The following validation scripts will be created to assist with the verification process:

1. `server_validation.sh`: Verify server access, disk mounts, and network configuration
2. `database_validation.sh`: Test database connections and basic functionality
3. `monitoring_validation.sh`: Verify monitoring system functionality
4. `backup_validation.sh`: Test backup and recovery procedures
5. `security_validation.sh`: Check security configurations
6. `performance_benchmark.sh`: Run basic performance tests
